# security-audits — .gitignore
# Goal: never commit downloaded/suspect code, secrets, or private working
# notes to version control (especially if this is ever pushed to a fork).

# ── Downloaded / suspect code under review ───────────────────────────
# Stage code you're statically reviewing in quarantine/. Its contents are
# never committed. NEVER build or run anything from here on your main
# machine — use the isolated Phase 5 environment (VM / throwaway account).
quarantine/*
!quarantine/README.md

# ── Private authorship-evidence: chat-session transcripts ────────────
# Development session transcripts are kept as PRIVATE evidence, never
# published. The folder's README is tracked; the transcripts are not.
provenance/*
!provenance/README.md

# Other scratch spaces
scratch/
samples/
tmp/

# Leftover per-target folders from the old convention
*_ORPHAN/

# ── Private / sensitive working notes you don't want on a fork ────────
private/
*.private.md
*.local.md

# ── Generated printable artifacts (derived from the .md source) ───────
# Printables are regenerated on demand from the Markdown that sits beside
# them. Committing them risks publishing a stale copy that someone prints
# and works from. Keep the Markdown as the single source of truth.
*.pdf
*.docx
*.rtf

# ── Secrets & credentials (defense in depth — should never live here) ─
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keychain
id_rsa*
*_rsa
*.token
secrets.*

# ── macOS / editor cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
.AppleDouble
*.swp
*~
